From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 05:16:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: describe ATC2 as a
 DisplayPort-only PHY

ATC2 has no USB controller on the J604: the ADT names it atc2-dpphy,
the fixed DisplayPort PHY behind the HDMI port. Describe it with its
five banks only (core, AXI2AF, LIOA, fabric and common configuration),
without the USB2 PHY and PIPE windows, so that the PHY driver runs it
as a four-lane DisplayPort PHY and never touches a USB block.

The SoC node is named after its first, USB2 PHY, window; a node whose
first window is the core bank is named phy@413000000, so the board file
deletes the SoC node and describes the PHY again (dtc W=1 simple_bus_reg
stays clean). The bank addresses are those of the t8132.dtsi atcphy2
node; the label, the alias and the dcpext0 links are unchanged. m1n1
already copies the T8132 calibration through the atcphy2 alias this
file declares; the DisplayPort-only PHY uses its bank and AUX lists.

The port stays disabled with dcpext0.

[j604: no upstream commit exists. Bank addresses as in d08e68a61c (from
 the J604 ADT atc-phy2 reg, measured on 2026-11-04); m1n1 copy path:
 omacom m1n1 kboot_atc.c dt_copy_t8132_usb3_tunables() for every
 atcphyN alias of an apple,t8132-atcphy node (CODE).]

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-hdmi.dtsi | 52 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 40 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-hdmi.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-hdmi.dtsi
index 029a428d4c..6efa5c176f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-hdmi.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-hdmi.dtsi
@@ -22,10 +22,15 @@
  * selector dcpext0 uses on every ATC crossbar. dcpext0 keeps its Type-C
  * routes.
  *
- * Everything here stays disabled with dcpext0 (t8132-j604-dcpext.dtsi): no
- * driver in this tree drives a T8132 external coprocessor, and the T8132 ATC
- * PHY has no DisplayPort mode outside USB4 tunnels yet. ATC2's power domains
- * (t8132-j604-pmgr.dtsi) stay disabled as well.
+ * ATC2 is described with its five banks only (ADT atc-phy2 reg: core, AXI2AF,
+ * LIOA, fabric, common configuration; no USB2 PHY or PIPE window), so the PHY
+ * driver runs it as a four-lane DisplayPort PHY. m1n1 copies its calibration
+ * through the atcphy2 alias like that of the USB-C ports' PHYs; the PHY uses
+ * the bank and AUX lists of it.
+ *
+ * Everything here stays disabled with dcpext0 (t8132-j604-dcpext.dtsi) until
+ * the external coprocessor driver path is enabled for the J604. ATC2's power
+ * domains (t8132-j604-pmgr.dtsi) stay disabled as well.
  *
  * The port's audio is DPA1 (ADT dp-audio1, SIO channel 0x66, the dp-audio
  * node dcpext0 names), as on the M3 Pro HDMI port. It is not described: this
@@ -41,15 +46,38 @@
 	};
 };
 
-&atcphy2 {
-	ports {
-		#address-cells = <1>;
-		#size-cells = <0>;
+/*
+ * The SoC node describes ATC2 with its USB windows and is named after the
+ * first of them. No USB controller uses ATC2 on this board: describe it again
+ * from its core bank, DisplayPort only (see above).
+ */
+/delete-node/ &atcphy2;
+
+&soc {
+	atcphy2: phy@413000000 {
+		compatible = "apple,t8132-atcphy";
+		reg = <0x4 0x13000000 0x0 0x24000>,
+		      <0x4 0x10000000 0x0 0x8000>,
+		      <0x4 0x10020000 0x0 0x4000>,
+		      <0x4 0x13044000 0x0 0x4000>,
+		      <0x4 0x13050000 0x0 0x4000>;
+		reg-names = "core", "axi2af", "lioa", "fabric", "common-config";
+		#phy-cells = <1>;
+		#reset-cells = <0>;
+		orientation-switch;
+		mode-switch;
+		power-domains = <&ps_atc2_usb>;
+		status = "disabled";
+
+		ports {
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
 
-		port@2 {
-			reg = <2>;
-			atcphy2_dp: endpoint {
-				remote-endpoint = <&dcpext0_dpout>;
+			port@2 {
+				reg = <2>;
+				atcphy2_dp: endpoint {
+					remote-endpoint = <&dcpext0_dpout>;
+				};
 			};
 		};
 	};
